WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
A strawberry plant sends out a
runner, and a new plant grows from it.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.790
That new plant is a clone:
genetically identical to its parent,

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.050
made by mitosis alone.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.450
Nine-banded armadillos usually give
birth to identical quadruplets,

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.250
all from one embryo.

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.260
But those clones begin in an early embryo.

7
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.370
Can one cell from an adult animal's
body be used to make an entire animal?

8
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.630
In this mission, you'll see how
growers turn one plant into thousands,

9
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.910
from tiny pieces of tissue.

10
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.220
Then you'll weigh the arguments
for and against cloning,

11
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.140
including a banana a
fungus largely wiped out.

12
00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:44.240
Your mission: find out whether one adult
body cell can be used to make an entire

13
00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:44.930
animal.
